{
  "rationale": "Model sensing and motion as separate plants, then use compact specifications to enforce a safe exploration policy with one-shot action states. The policy prioritizes move_forward in clear space, uses occasional random_walk for coverage variation, routes every obstacle event through dedicated recovery states, uses move_backward only for front-obstacle escape, and reserves full_rotate for a dedicated last-resort stuck state after repeated front blockage.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate uncontrollable perception from controllable motion capability",
    "Use decision and one-shot commit/recovery states so uncontrollable events are total while each action state enables exactly one controllable",
    "Bias clear-space behavior toward forward motion, with occasional random_walk but no steady turning in place",
    "Handle obstacle_left with rotate_clockwise and obstacle_right with rotate_counterclockwise consistently",
    "Handle obstacle_front via brief backward escape then directed turn, escalating to full_rotate only through a dedicated stuck helper path"
  ],
